From 6eafcd41e9cf526d8f5cf60a835b5142e7fce94c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: arm64: scope the translation cache to one app;
 count queued records

For step P3 of the persistent translation cache (ANAL-381), on patch 13: a
G14 test turns the cache on for its test app without turning it on for
any other app that starts meanwhile, and can tell how many records were
still waiting when an app was stopped.

- berberis.pcache also takes on:<package> and verify:<package>: the cache
  is on only in processes of that package, by exact name
  (GetAppPackageName, which native_bridge_initialize sets from the private
  directory before InitBerberis). A process without a package name, any
  other package, and a malformed value (an empty or invalid name, another
  mode, extra fields) stay off. off, on and verify are unchanged. The scope
  is decided once, at initialization.
- New counters pcache_records_queued and pcache_records_dropped. A record is
  counted as queued under the write queue's lock, when it's published and
  appended; dropped when its batch isn't written (the cap, a file that
  would pass 4 GiB, a failed or no longer owned write, a fork child).
  Queued - written - dropped, read from a running app's counter block,
  estimates what's waiting: the counters aren't read as one snapshot, and
  it isn't the number lost at a later kill. Drops at the cap and at 4 GiB
  were counted as not persistable; they're dropped now.

Tests: PersistentCacheConfig.ScopedValuesTurnTheCacheOnForTheirPackageOnly
(exact match, prefix, case, no identity, twelve malformed values);
PersistentCacheTest.QueuedWrittenAndDroppedAccountForEveryRecord; the cap
and 4 GiB tests check the dropped count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-authored-by: multica-agent <github@multica.ai>
